      <methods>
         <methodStep>
            <description>
               <para>DATA DESCRIPTION: Each 6.25 m2 plot was cleared of woody debris in fall 1995 and first measured in 1996. Dry weight of coarse litterfall (&gt;2 cm diameter) deposited in the plots from live trees is measured each year (May-June). CWD from dead or fallen trees is not collected. Spruce/fir zone plots were established in 2001 and first measured in 2002. Samples are dried for a week at 60C.</para>
               <para>SAMPLING DESIGN: Six plots, each 2.5 x 2.5 m (6.26 m2), are located adjacent to fine litterfall collectors. Locations of the five sample sites were chosen to stratify the sampling by elevation zone.</para>
            </description>
         </methodStep>
      </methods>
